{:edb/db-before-t 1138 :edb/db-after-t 1139 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534451 50 #inst "2026-10-07T05:02:48.114Z" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183892 1100 "Calculate  $\\displaystyle{\\int x^2 e^{x^3+1}\\, \\textrm{d}x }.$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183892 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int x^2 e^{x^3+1}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534451 false] [17592186183892 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable\n\n$$\nu = x^3+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm{d}u = x^2 \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\intx^{2}e^{x^{3} + 1}dx &= \\inte^{x^{3} + 1} \\cdot x^{2}dx \\\\\n&= \\inte^{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}\\inte^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}e^{u} + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{3}e^{x^{3} + 1} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 false] [17592186183892 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable $u = x^3+1.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 3x^2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm{d}u = x^2 \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{{x}^{3}+1}\\cdot \\,{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{{x}^{3}+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183893 1100 "Calculate  $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183893 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534451 false] [17592186183893 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable $u= 1-x^4$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x} = -4x^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\textrm{d}u\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} \\int {x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}}}\\, \\textrm{d}x &=\\int {{3^{1-x^4}}\\cdot x^3}\\, \\textrm{d}x \\\\[5pt] &= \\int {3^{u}} \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\int {3^{u}} \\textrm{d}u \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C \\\\[5pt] &= -\\dfrac{3^{1-x^4}}{4\\ln 3}+ C. \\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 false] [17592186183893 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable $u= 1-x^4.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{ \\textrm{d}u}{ \\textrm{d}x} = -4x^3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad x^3 \\, \\textrm{d}x = -\\dfrac{1}{4} \\textrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\int {x^3\\,{3^{1-x^4}} }\\, \\textrm{d}x \n&=\\int {{3^{1-x^4}}\\cdot x^3 }\\, \\textrm{d}x \\[5pt]\n&=  \\int {3^{u}} \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{4}\\right) \\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n                                                     &= -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\int {3^{u}}  \\textrm{d}u\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=  -\\dfrac{1}{4}\\cdot\\dfrac{3^{u}}{\\ln 3} + C\\[5pt]\n                                                     &=   -\\dfrac{3^{1-x^4}}{4\\ln 3}+ C.\n}\n$$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183894 1100 "Calculate  $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x.$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183894 1100 "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac {e^{2x}} {e^{2x} + 1} \\, \\textrm{d}x$." 13194139534451 false] [17592186183894 1145 "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable\n\n$$\nu = e^{2x}+1\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\dfrac{1}{2}\\, \\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\frac{e^{2x}}{e^{2x} + 1}dx &= \\int\\frac{1}{e^{2x} + 1} \\cdot e^{2x}dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{u} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\int\\frac{1}{u}du \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}u & + C \\\\ = \\frac{1}{2}\\ln & e^{2x} + 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}\\ln (e^{2x} + 1) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x$." 13194139534451 false] [17592186183894 1145 "Notice that the numerator is proportional to the derivative of the denominator. So, we introduce the new variable $u = e^{2x}+1.$ Differentiating gives \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}= 2e^{2x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\\, \\textrm{d}u = e^{2x} \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x}}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{{e}^{2x}+1}\\cdot {e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{e}^{2x}+1|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2x}+1)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that, in the last step, we used the fact that $e^{2x} + 1 > 0$ for all $x.$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186183895 1100 "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt {\\ln 4}} 16xe^{-2x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534451 false] [17592186183895 1100 "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle{\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt {\\ln 4}} 16xe^{-2x^2}\\, \\textrm{d}x}$." 13194139534451 true] [17592186183895 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable $u=-2x^2$. Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-4x \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad -4 \\, \\textrm{d}u=16x \\, \\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt {\\ln 4}$ |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\ln 4}}16xe^{-2x^{2}}dx &= \\int_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\ln 4}}e^{-2x^{2}} \\cdot 16xdx \\\\\n&= \\int_{0}^{-2\\ln 4}e^{u} \\cdot (-4du) \\\\\n&=-4\\int_{0}^{-2\\ln 4}e^{u}du \\\\\n&= \\left.- 4e^{u}\\right|_{0}^{-2\\ln 4} \\\\\n&=-4(e^{-2\\ln 4} - e^{0}) \\\\\n&=-4(\\frac{1}{16} - 1) \\\\\n&= 4(\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{15}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 false] [17592186183895 1145 "Let's introduce the new variable $u=-2x^2.$ Differentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}u}{\\textrm{d}x}=-4x\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\n-4 \\, \\textrm{d}u=16x \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, we determine the new limits of integration:\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\sqrt {\\ln 4}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $-2\\ln 4$ |\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}16x{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}}{e}^{-2{x}^{2}}\\cdot 16x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}\\cdot (-4\\,\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =-4{\\int }_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-4{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4} \\\\  & =-4({e}^{-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =-4(\\frac{1}{16}-1) \\\\  & =4(\\frac{15}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534451 true] [17592186184293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288958 13194139534451 true] [17592186184293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288972 13194139534451 true] [17592186184293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289032 13194139534451 true] [17592186184293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289039 13194139534451 true] [17592186184293 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289060 13194139534451 true] [17592186184294 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288965 13194139534451 true] [17592186184294 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288993 13194139534451 true] [17592186184294 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289046 13194139534451 true] [17592186184294 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289067 13194139534451 true] [17592186184295 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289000 13194139534451 true] [17592186184295 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289007 13194139534451 true] [17592186184295 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289025 13194139534451 true] [17592186184295 1020 #edb/ref 17592186289053 13194139534451 true] [17592186184296 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288979 13194139534451 true] [17592186184296 1020 #edb/ref 17592186288986 1319413953